in his acceptance speech overnight  president-elect Donald Trump said  America needs to come together and quote  bind the wounds of division he also  promised to be the president for all  people on 60 minutes Sunday CBS News  contributor and Republican strategist  Frank Luntz gathered a focus group of  undecided voters it revealed how deep  those divisions are how do we get to the  point where every one of you with  different backgrounds different politics  different objectives all of you gave me  a negative reaction how did we get the  election how did we get here it's our  fault  you saw it here everybody's arguing I'm  afraid to even bring up a point  I'm not Pro Trump but I see why people  like it and you know if I say that I'm  gonna be you know ostracized my biggest  fear is that these candidates aren't a  mistake that the American people have  elected the future of America what we  aspire to be and what we are deep down  inside I think Trump has gotten so much  traction at this point because deep down  inside there are a lot of Americans that  feel the exact same way as that deep  down are cont our country is divided I'm  sorry we're not united we are at each  other's throats and I'm sorry maybe this  is what it is maybe this is the  candidates that we want Frank Luntz  joins us at the table there was so much  negativity with the group last night in  that group that you showed us on 60  minutes and last night Donald Trump has  promised to unite us when some so many  people believe he's the one that helped  divide this country how was he able to  prove or how was he able to prove to  people that I'm the one who can turn  things around how is he able to do that  well first last night's speech was the  best speech I've seen Donald Trump give  it truly was magnanimous he was reaching  out he said the kinds of commitments  that I was hoping he would say and he  appeared to be serious and if you doubt  it right and even his not well I doubt  everything about politics right now  let's start with the exit polls because  I'm a pollster yeah virtually every  state was wrong that they predicted  either the wrong winner or they were off  by four or five in Ohio is almost 10% it  was off why because Donald Trump  don't even want to participate in polls  they don't want to tell pollsters what  they're doing not because they're afraid  but because they're uncooperative  they're so hostile to the system that  they feel like that is giving in well  Donald Trump's campaign paid millions of  dollars to an overseas firm it is called  Cambridge analytic a five million  dollars in September alone  they used data points from gym  memberships from transactions on loyalty  cards charity donations all to target  their voters and the data people that  worked for Cambridge analytic assay they  knew over ten days ago that they might  win this election so are the pollsters  wrong and there's something there's  another new way to gather data out there  that the political class hasn't picked  up on yet you have to be able to read  people when they don't necessarily tell  you who they're going to vote for that  there are other things as part of the  decision-making process  Osama team did that in 2008 2012 they  said we can tell about what kind of car  you buy we can target you watch a  micro-targeting but but the issue now is  when you have when you are so upset with  the way things are going when you think  Washington has betrayed you and Wall  Street has betrayed you then you  absolutely you're not going to cooperate  and you're gonna find some other way to  express your point of view now I went to  a couple of Trump rallies on Monday and  what I saw were people who not only  couldn't wait to vote but they were  going to drag 1015 people with them  where was that the level of intensity in  Pennsylvania which he won and in North  Carolina which he won Hillary Clinton we  forget that Hillary Clinton was actually  not a good candidate in a traditional  election being first lady's Secretary of  State and senator would absolutely  qualify you and would probably propel  you to the presidency but if you have an  American electorate that is so angry  with the system and so angry with the  elites as part of the system that's  actually negative - yeah we hear that  she was not a good candidate before last  night absolutely like I'm hearing that  more and more last night until then  everyone you know she was Hillary  Clinton the most qualified candidate the  best suited for the job the best  temperament now is not a good candidate  that is being qualified and being a  great bringing a good candidate I  so she had a 43 42 percent favorability  rating before 53 54 percent didn't like  her we forgot that we weren't talking  about the fact that she had the highest  negativity of any Democratic nominee and  now we are being reminded of it and one  more we did a survey last night 1200  voters and we asked them if it was  Bernie Sanders versus Donald Trump who  would win by 8 points they preferred  Bernie Sanders over Donald Trump and the  reason why character we want to say that  elections are about policy they aren't  they're actually about who do you trust  who do you have more faith in and who do  you think understand you but you think  this election was more about character  or change I think was more about change  and it's not just changed in terms of  policy it's in terms of trust and they  simply didn't trust her and the exit  polls which I don't want to cite ever  again but even the exit polls talked  about the lack of trust in Hillary but  they also said that change was the most  important driving factor right and  that's why I don't understand why they  were so wrong why they had Clinton  winning in state after state that Trump  actually won this is a very interesting  I think it's actually a very good day  for democracy and it's a very bad day  for pollsters do you can tie yourself up  polls of course not okay I did yesterday  but today on our communication  specialist okay got it got it Frank  always reinvent yourself yeah yeah and I  have to do it every week so I'd become  good at it Jake Communications got it  okay thank you so much thank you

